   "source": [
    "# Exploratory Data Analysis of BTC & ETH (2023–2025)\n",
    "\n",
    "## Executive Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "In this project, our team explored the historical trends of Bitcoin (BTC) and Ethereum (ETH) from 2023 to 2025 using data collected from the CryptoCompare API.\n",
    "\n",
    "Our main goal was to understand how these two major cryptocurrencies have performed over time in terms of price movement, volatility, and correlation.\n",
    "\n",
    "We used Python to collect, clean, and analyze the data through Pandas and Matplotlib. The process included converting timestamps, calculating daily returns, visualizing price trends, and comparing the two coins statistically. Through this exploratory data analysis (EDA), we identified key patterns and insights about how BTC and ETH behave individually and in relation to each other.\n",
    "\n",
    "Overall, we found that both cryptocurrencies follow similar long-term trends but differ in short-term volatility and price stability.\n"
   ]
  },
